<%#
  A snapshot row is marked with the brand tint rather than a hex literal.

  **Its cells were one column out of true.** The whole location-and-quantity dump was rendered in
  the *From location* cell, with To location and Items left empty -- so the one row on the page
  that lists items put them under a heading that says where things moved from, and it stood 97px
  tall against 55px for every other row. A snapshot is not a movement: it has no from and no to.
  The breakdown belongs in Items, which is where every other row lists "item: quantity", and the
  two movement columns are empty because there is nothing to put in them.
%>
<tr class="bg-brand-50">
  <td><%= event.user&.name || "Not recorded" %></td>
  <td>Snapshot</td>
  <td></td>
  <%# The same format as every other row. `to_s` gave this one column two date formats. %>
  <td><%= event.event_time.strftime("%Y/%m/%d %H:%M:%S %Z") %></td>
  <td></td>
  <td></td>
  <td>
    <% event.data.storage_locations.values.each do |loc| %>
      <%= link_to storage_locs.find { |i| i.id == loc.id}.name, storage_location_path(loc.id), class: "font-medium text-brand-700 hover:text-brand-800" %>
      <% loc.items.values.each do |entry| %>
        <% item = items.find { |i| i.id == entry.item_id} %>
        <% if item %>
          <%= link_to items.find { |i| i.id == entry.item_id}.name, item_path(entry.item_id), class: "font-medium text-brand-700 hover:text-brand-800" %>:
        <% else %>
          Item <%= entry.item_id %> (deleted)
        <% end %>
        <%= entry.quantity %>
      <% end %>
      <br>
    <% end %>
  </td>
  <%# No actions: a snapshot has no `eventable` to narrow the history to. The cell is still here,
      because a row short of a cell would pull the frozen actions column out of line. %>
  <td class="cell-actions"></td>
</tr>
